# .rules — Bonjou CLI

## Project Overview

Bonjou is a terminal-based LAN chat and file-transfer CLI application written in Go. It discovers peers via UDP broadcast on port 46320 and exchanges messages and files over TCP on port 46321. No server, no internet required. The binary runs as a single long-lived process with a readline-based prompt and an event-driven TUI layer built on the Charmbracelet stack. Bonjou targets macOS, Windows, and major Linux environments, so user-visible behavior must remain consistent across all three platforms.

All source lives under `cmd/` (entry point) and `internal/` (all packages). There are no tests, no CI/CD pipelines, and no linter configuration files in the repository.

